q 0.000 g BT 59.53 641.58 Td (Virtual test suites are not like a traditional test suite defined by the XML suite specification. Virtual test) Tj ET Q
q 0.000 g BT 59.53 627.41 Td (suites are dynamically generated in real-time by the Benchy client based upon the specified test critera.) Tj ET Q
q 0.000 g BT 59.53 613.24 Td (Virtual test suites can automatically consist of all test profiles that are compatible with a particular) Tj ET Q
q 0.000 g BT 59.53 599.06 Td (operating system or test profiles that meet other critera. When running a virtual suite, the) Tj ET Q
q 0.000 g BT 59.53 584.89 Td (OpenBenchmarking.org repository of the test profiles to use for generating the dynamic suite must be) Tj ET Q
q 0.000 g BT 59.53 570.72 Td (prefixed. ) Tj ET Q
BT /F2 11.00 Tf ET
q 0.000 g BT 59.53 542.37 Td (Virtual test suites can be installed and run just like a normal XML test suite and shares nearly all of the) Tj ET Q
q 0.000 g BT 59.53 528.20 Td (same capabilities. However, when running a virtual suite, the user will be prompted to input any) Tj ET Q
q 0.000 g BT 59.53 514.02 Td (user-configuration options for needed test profiles just as they would need to do if running the test) Tj ET Q
q 0.000 g BT 59.53 499.85 Td (individually. When running a virtual suite, the user also has the ability to select individual tests within the) Tj ET Q
q 0.000 g BT 59.53 485.68 Td (suite to run or to run all of the contained test profiles. Virtual test suites are also only supported for an) Tj ET Q
q 0.000 g BT 59.53 471.50 Td (OpenBenchmarking.org repository if there is no test profile or test suite of the same name in the) Tj ET Q
q 0.000 g BT 59.53 457.33 Td (repository. Below is a list of common virtual test suites for the main Phoronix Test Suite repository, but) Tj ET Q
q 0.000 g BT 59.53 443.16 Td (the dynamic list of available virtual test suites based upon the enabled repositories is available by) Tj ET Q
